  "live_records": {
    "q-184998": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184998",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the following false statement.\n\n$3n-1$ is odd for any $n\\in Z$ \n\nA counterexample for this statement would be an integer {{field-1}} such that {{field-2}} is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,3n-1\\text{ is odd}.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,3n-1\\text{ is odd})\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,3n-1\\text{ is even}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that $3n-1$ is $\\text{even}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
